<title>INDIA: India's Dena Bank to launch equity issue.</title>
<headline>India's Dena Bank to launch equity issue.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian state-run Dena Bank said on Thursday it would raise 18 million rupees through an initial equity offering later this month.</p>
<p>Dena Bank officials told a news conference the 10 rupee face value shares would be priced at a premium of 20 rupees each.</p>
<p>They said the issue price of 30 rupees a share is based on its 1995/96 (April-March) earnings per share of 3.52 rupees and reflects a price earnings multiple of 8.52.</p>
<p>The issue will open for subscription on October 28.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
